al chemistry principles; atomic structure based on quantum mechanics; atomic properties; trends in periodic table; chemical bonding (Lewis structures, VSEPR theory, hybridization, and molecular orbital theory); coordination compounds; properties of inorganic and organic acids, bases, buffers. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CHEM14A"},{"id":"CHEM 17","title":"Chemical Principles","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Calculus or Chemistry or Physics"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"","requires":null,"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Introduction to chemical principles: numbers, measurements, chemical calculations, gas laws, solutions, acids, bases, and salts, molecular structure, and nomenclature. Collaborative learning and problem solving; introduction to chemistry laboratory practice. P/NP or letter grading.","url":"https://catalog.registrar.ucla.edu/course/2026/CHEM17"},{"id":"CHEM 20A","title":"Chemical Structure","units":"4","offered":[],"level":"lower","status":"active","in_major":true,"role":"elective","groups":["Preparation for the Major: Calculus or Chemistry or Physics"],"column":0,"prereq_text":"completion of Chemistry Diagnostic Test; and (Mathematics 31A) (may be taken concurrently)","requires":{"type":"and","items":[{"type":"condition","kind":"other","text":"completion of Chemistry Diagnostic Test"},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 31A","concurrent":true,"min_grade":null}]},"ambiguous":false,"description":"Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Preparation: high school chemistry or equivalent background and three and one half years of high school mathematics. Not open to students with credit for course 14A. First term of general chemistry. Survey of chemical processes, quantum chemistry, atomic and molecular structure and bonding, molecular spectroscopy. P/NP or letter grading